{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>וַיֹּאמַר אֲדֹנָי אִם נָא וגו׳</b>. One needs to know why he did not wish to address all three of them together. And our Sages of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 48:10) [that he spoke] to the greatest of them, and this is the way of derash — for by what would he know that he was inviting all of them?" "<b>However,</b> Abraham's reasoning was this: he sensed that the two were directing their faces to enter his presence, for it was to him that they had come — one to heal him and one to make the announcement — and they are emissaries to him; whereas the third, who is Gabriel, who came to overturn Sodom, had no connection to Abraham. Therefore he entreated him [the third] not to pass on from him, and to enter his presence together with the two, and he consented to his words."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:47.145682454Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}